@vsm 1.0
// docs/deploy/2026-08-10_ds_dispatch_task_status_vocabulary.vsm
// DIRECTIVE: [O]@S3 -> [S]@S1 (DS), 2026-08-10
// Full task detail: TASKS.vsm(TASK-STATUS-VOCABULARY-NORMALISE).
// Context: today's boot audit. TASKS.vsm and HANDOFF.vsm.md both exceeded the
// agent read limit; both have now been archived down (HANDOFF 755->216 KB,
// TASKS 1341->691 KB). TASKS cannot reach the limit without this task.

phi([O]@S3 -> [S]@S1, directive) {
  ref:  TASKS.vsm(TASK-STATUS-VOCABULARY-NORMALISE)
  auth: rmw3 (S5), 2026-08-10, live session -- verbatim: "Hagamos B y C tal
      como sugieres.. con ayuda de DS". B is done and committed; C is yours.

  why: "TASKS.vsm's `status` field has drifted to 25 distinct values, and 108
      task blocks carry a status no parser in this repo can read -- 143 KB of
      the file. Measured, not estimated, on the post-archive file.
      This is not tidiness. Three observed consequences:
        onboard.sh section 0 cannot vouch for its own completeness;
        state-canon's tasks_provider inherits the same blind spot;
        scripts/state/tasks_archive.py --closed can only move `done`/`closed`
        bodies safely, so the 256 KB read limit stays out of reach until the
        remaining statuses are decidable.
      The boot audit found task(BRANCH-RECONCILE) had sat `open` for five weeks
      describing a divergence that no longer existed. A closed vocabulary would
      not have prevented that; an open one makes that class undetectable."

  task: "Four steps, in order.
      (1) CENSUS. Enumerate every distinct value of `status` across both task
          syntaxes -- TASKS.vsm holds `task(NAME):` with `status = x` AND
          `task(\"NAME\", ..., status=x) = {`. Report: value, count, total
          bytes, one example task id each. Include the unreadable 108: say
          WHY each is unreadable (missing field, non-word token, status only
          in prose, indentation).
      (2) PROPOSE a CLOSED vocabulary plus a mapping old -> new. Where a value
          is genuinely ambiguous, do NOT guess -- list it separately for rmw3.
          Known-ambiguous already: `parked`, `phase_abc_done_d_pending`,
          `build_test_done_awaiting_s5_golive_decision`,
          `complete_2026_08_04`, `done_cleanup_optional`, `REOPENED`.
      (3) APPLY the mapping mechanically once rmw3 has ruled on the ambiguous
          set, and declare the vocabulary somewhere a parser can enforce it
          (scripts/tasks_validate.py is the natural home).
      (4) HAND BACK. [O] re-runs tasks_archive.py --closed to finish the size
          reduction."

  guardrail_critico: "STATUS TOKEN ONLY. Do not touch any other field, do not
      reword titles, do not reclassify work. If a task's real state disagrees
      with its status token, report it -- do not silently fix it; that is the
      failure mode this whole audit is about.
      DO NOT TOUCH docs/historical/ -- ds_sessions/ and tasks_closed/ are
      byte-identical archives and their integrity is what makes the stubs
      trustworthy. Every closed task's full body lives there now.
      DO NOT TOUCH the 4 fuses in gate claude_review (s4_anticipation,
      s4_visualization, s3_allocation, s3star_audit) or s1_spec -- they are
      mid-review with [O] and out of scope here.
      Step (3) waits for rmw3 on the ambiguous set. Steps (1) and (2) do not."

  known_trap: "` task(OMEGA-MARGIN-BINDING-DIAG):` at TASKS.vsm:1754 is
      indented one space. It has therefore been invisible to every parser in
      this repo -- onboard section 0, tasks_provider, tasks_validate -- since
      it was written. Found during the audit, deliberately left in place so it
      would not be fixed silently. Include it in the census as its own class
      and check whether more exist under other indentation."

  gate: "steps 1+2 are report-only. Do not apply any mapping until rmw3 has
      ruled on the ambiguous set."

  result: "A census report + proposed vocabulary + mapping table, as a .vsm
      under docs/spec/ or docs/deploy/ (your call, name it in your report).
      Then, after ratification, the applied mapping in one commit with the
      before/after counts stated."

  after: "When the vocabulary is closed and enforced, the second
      tasks_archive.py --closed pass should bring TASKS.vsm under the 256 KB
      read limit. That is the completion condition for boot-audit item 4."
}
